 "deviations": [
  "D1 holes use the body_v2 print tolerances (task rule): M3 through 3.3 (spec 3.2), M3 tap in PLA 2.8 (spec 2.5 for the nose column), M2x8 pilots 1.7 (A); horizontal holes are teardrops (45 deg roof) for the upright prints",
  "D2 nose: base flange r 57.76-60 x 1.8 joins the skirt (r 57.76-58.6) to the shell (r >= 59.16) - the massing touched nowhere there (0.56 mm radial gap); its outer 1.4 mm is a flat overhang ring in the tip-up print (P2S prints it, not 45 deg)",
  "D3 the payload_bulkhead spring boss (d 30 x 8, r 14.16-15) cannot be printed with 'flat, ribs up' (it stands on the bed face) -> separate flanged spring_seat ring (flange under the first coil, spring force keeps it); the pusher tether ties to 2 x D1.8 holes in the bulkhead plate instead of the boss",
  "D4 nose ballast pocket: closed by a 45 deg cone (r 12 at z 784 -> r 3 at z 793) instead of the massing's open-topped tube (it floated 0.9 mm off the shell); capacity +1.5 cm3; the pocket tube and column still need the supports in the pocket mouth the spec allows",
  "D5 GPS mount: the two 45 deg ledges (rev 3 F3) are replaced by two slotted side ribs whose slot floors carry the ground plane (z 580) and whose free inner fingers carry the 2 printed snap lips (spec: 'slotted cradle + 2 snap hooks')",
  "D6 raceways = continuous helical tunnels with the spec cross-sections (release 5 x 2.5, GPS 4 x 3, walls 0.84) and a 1.5 mm lead slit on the inner face (the factory plugs 8.15 x 4 / 7.5 x 4.3 cannot be threaded through a closed 5 x 2.5 / 4 x 3 tunnel); GPS tunnel 62 deg from vertical gets a 45 deg web to the skin; both ends clipped by a 45 deg cone",
  "D7 release-servo cradle: 2 pillars (t 11.7-17.5, r 47-59.6) under the ears at the F hole pitch 28.0 + a back web r 56.7 behind the case (massing: bosses at +-13.75 and a top plate r 53-59.3 that overlapped the MG90S case r 44-56.5)",
  "D8 sleeve 'snaps onto the pusher' drawn as a 3-lug bayonet (20 deg twist) - a plain snap hook on the 2.4 ring strains PLA ~5 %; the pusher outer ring gets 3 notches (r 29.5-31.9, 6 wide)",
  "D9 nose shell is blunted with the F tip radius 3.0 (tangent sphere): apex lies below z 800 by the value in the check",
  "D10 rail tops get a 3 mm 45 deg lead-in on the inner edge (CanSat / sleeve insertion); nose skirt 0.6 lead-in chamfer"
 ],
